       Condition  attributes  can  be specified at condition creation time, by
       passing  a  condition  attribute   object   as   second   argument   to
       pptthhrreeaadd__ccoonndd__iinniitt(3).   Passing  NULL is equivalent to passing a condi‐
       tion attribute object with all attributes set to their default values.

       The LinuxThreads implementation supports no attributes for  conditions.
       The  functions on condition attributes are included only for compliance
       with the POSIX standard.

       pptthhrreeaadd__ccoonnddaattttrr__iinniitt() initializes the condition attribute object _a_t_t_r
       and fills it with default  values  for  the  attributes.   pptthhrreeaadd__ccoonn‐‐
       ddaattttrr__ddeessttrrooyy()  destroys  a condition attribute object, which must not
       be reused until it is reinitialized.  Both functions do nothing in  the
       LinuxThreads implementation.

